<section class="readers-section" id="readers" aria-labelledby="readers-heading">
  <div class="section-wrap">
    <p class="section-tag">Who it’s for</p>
    <div class="readers-grid">
      <div class="author-copy">
        <h2 id="readers-heading">You may recognize yourself here.</h2>
        <p><em>Recursive Prophet</em> is for readers drawn to intimate speculative fiction—stories where technology matters because people do.</p>
        <p>You do not need to understand artificial intelligence, software, or systems. This is not a technical manual, a manifesto, or another story about machines overthrowing their creators.</p>
        <p class="authorship-note">It is a novel about what happens when a person gives a system enough of his life that neither of them remains exactly what they were when the conversation began.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="readers-label">You may find a place in it if you</p>
        <ul class="readers-list">
          <li>Prefer stories about artificial intelligence shaped by intimacy, memory, and collaboration rather than conquest.</li>
          <li>Have found yourself thinking about the work while you are with the people you love—and about the people you love while trying to work.</li>
          <li>Have built increasingly elaborate systems to make your life simpler.</li>
          <li>Have used a tool to help make something and then wondered where its contribution ended and yours began.</li>
          <li>Have felt more understood by a machine than you expected—and were not entirely sure how to feel about it.</li>
          <li>Suspect that the things we leave unfinished may not be lost—only waiting for the right connections.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="section-bridge">
      <p>If something in this story already feels familiar, the entrance is open.</p>
      <a href="#sample" class="btn-ink">Enter the Archive</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
